+++ b/CHANGES/v2.11.md
@@ -449,6 +449,12 @@ The entries below give the details; the main cases are:
 
 #### Core, performance and input
 
+  - Less work for every action that uses atoms at every step: the periodic boundary conditions are copied into the action only when the box changes
+    (and are not recomputed when the MD code passes the same box), and constant masses and charges are copied only once.
+    With 200 [DISTANCE](DISTANCE.md) the calculation is about 18% faster, with 20 [GYRATION](GYRATION.md) of 1000 atoms about 4%.
+
+  - Making the molecules whole no longer opens an OpenMP parallel region when it runs on one thread, which happens for every action with few atoms
+    (e.g. [DISTANCE](DISTANCE.md)) at every step. With 200 [DISTANCE](DISTANCE.md) and a [RESTRAINT](RESTRAINT.md) on them the calculation is almost twice as fast.
   - The virial of the collective variables that compute it from the atomic derivatives (e.g. [DISTANCE](DISTANCE.md), [GYRATION](GYRATION.md) and the multicolvars)
     is computed about four times faster: the loop over the atoms stalled on a temporary tensor. With 20 [GYRATION](GYRATION.md) of 1000 atoms the forward loop is 20% faster,
     with 200 [DISTANCE](DISTANCE.md) 10% faster. The results are identical.
